stx_minmallocpp

stx_minmallocpp is part of STXlib and is STXlib's own code, under STXlib's
licence (the repository's LICENSE). It is a conversion to house-style C++ of
the design of mimalloc v3 (https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc), by Daan
Leijen and Microsoft Corporation: thread heaps, pages of one block size,
the separation of the owner's frees from other threads' frees, the rule
that a full page is abandoned and claimed again by a later free, arenas cut
into slices, and an address map consulted without touching the address. No
source text of mimalloc is copied. By the owner's decision of 2026-11-15
it carries mimalloc's notice, which follows unchanged.

Its index of free slice runs is TLSF (M. Masmano, I. Ripoll, A. Crespo and
J. Real, "TLSF: a new dynamic memory allocator for real-time systems",
ECRTS 2004), implemented from the paper.

